  "preamble": "The shift from the open central/back vowel [a] to the near-open front vowel [æ] is a common historical process known as fronting or palatalization. It frequently occurs when influenced by surrounding palatal consonants or through broad systemic vowel shifts. In Russian, stressed /a/ is fronted to [æ] between soft (palatalized) consonants: пять [pʲætʲ] 'five', against сад [ˈsɑ̟ˑt̪] 'garden'.",
